ings  here are you want to make sure you do  this very cold pbs wash with the samples  to remove all the media  and then you want to target your lysis  solution on the cells  at about 100 cells per microliter  when you go and you actually uh send  your samples to the service provider  you're going to be sending them  uh probably in a 96 well plate if you're  already working in 384 well plates you  can do that as well  but we do request that you leave a  couple of walls blank so that we can add  some hela and liver rna controls and  these are batch processing controls  that allow us to see essentially what's  happening at the service provider  and when we talk about actually working  with a partner such as yourself  typically we go through these different  phases there's a pilot phase  here's again where we like to determine  that the cell line is actually working  with the lysis  under the right conditions in some cases  we might actually  do a second dilution in the lysis buffer  um and we might also adjust the ampli  amplification cycles that we're actually  using  should we be working with some very  different  type of cell this allows us to ensure  basically that everything is working  well up front then typically there'll be  a small  pop study where the customer will will  run  known compounds with known effects so  that we can uh basically demonstrate  uh the effectiveness of these  transcriptome profiles and we do all of  this again  ahead of the full screen and again these  screens can be quite large we're talking  uh in order of 10 uh to 40 000  samples in a screen um and that allows  us essentially to get down to  these very low cost price points  now we've partnered essentially this  service offering with ibx  here in the united states this is  formerly known as redcore  or or this was uh the rutgers  service uh provider they've recently  changed their name uh  to infinity biologics ibx uh however and  they are  in uh in new jersey uh so in the united  s